**Given:**

3a = 4b = 6c and a + b + c = 27sqrt{29}

Calculation:

3a = 4b = 6c

⇒ a ∶ b ∶ c 

⇒ 4 × 6 ∶ 3 × 6 ∶ 3 × 4 

⇒ 4 ∶ 3 ∶ 2 

According to the question, 

a + b + c = 27sqrt{29}

⇒ 4x + 3x + 2x = 27sqrt{29}

⇒ 9x = 27sqrt{29}

⇒ x = 3sqrt{29}

We have to find, 

 sqrt {{a²} + {b²} + {c²}} 

⇒ sqrt{{(4x)²}{{}} + {{}}{(3x)²}{{}} + {{}}{{{(2x)}}²}} 

⇒ sqrt{29x²}

⇒ xsqrt{29}

⇒ 3 × sqrt{29} × sqrt{29} = 87 

∴ The correct answer is 87.

